# mod-paragon-itemgen: the Cursed Altar (operator 2026-10-30/31). A warrior (Paragon 50, role dps / strength,
# spec Arms) gets a cursed rare chest and a plain rare chest. Away from the altar nothing happens; at the altar
# (Hall of the Guardian, map 736) the cursed chest is sacrificed for 5 Cursed Essence (rare yield) and its passive
# joins the account's collection; the plain chest is then bound to Mortal Strike +50% (950007, unlocked by the GM)
# for 30 Cursed Essence + 2 Tainted Heartstones (rare costs). Refusals: too little essence, a mage passive
# (950002 = +20% Intellect, in no warrior pool).
# Bag positions: the bot's backpack holds only its hearthstone in slot 1, so the two chests land in slots 2 and 3.
name    Paragon item gen - the Cursed Altar: sacrifice, collection, bind
timeout 120s

bot q warrior slot=25 paragon=50

place 0 -8828.0 647.0 94.3 0
require q alive
do q destroy 37612
do q destroy 37395
do q destroy 920300
do q destroy 920301
as q .paragon role dps
as q .paragon stat strength
# the role rows are written asynchronously; the roll reads them synchronously
wait 2s

# spec Arms at the Paragon Artificer (option 0 is the info line, 1 = Arms)
pick artificer creature:900100 near q
require artificer exists
# approach stops at 6.2 yd here (the gossip handler takes 5.5): step next to the NPC
do q goto -8823.0 640.0 94.2
wait 1s
do q gossip artificer option 1
expect output has Spec set to
wait 2s

do gm target q
as gm .additem 37612 1 cursed
as gm .additem 37395 1
wait 1s
expect q item 37612 == 1
expect q item 37395 == 1

# away from the altar
as q .paragon altar sacrifice 0 2
expect output has You must stand at the Cursed Altar
expect q item 37612 == 1

# at the altar
place 736 506.0 533.8 1212.89 3.14
require q map 736
as q .paragon altar list
expect output has at altar 1
expect output has sacrifice bag 0 slot 2: item 37612 enchant 95
expect output has target bag 0 slot 3: item 37395

as q .paragon altar sacrifice 0 2
expect output has crumbles into 5 Cursed Essence
# spec Arms: the curse carries a passive, so the sacrifice unlocks it (or names it as known on a rerun)
expect output lacks plain curse
expect q item 37612 == 0
expect q item 920300 == 5

do gm target q
as gm .paragon altar unlock 950007
expect output has unlocked

# 5 essence, a rare costs 30
as q .paragon altar bind 0 3 950007
expect output has You need 30 Cursed Essence

do gm target q
as gm .additem 920300 25
as gm .additem 920301 2
wait 1s
expect q item 920300 == 30
expect q item 920301 == 2

# a mage passive is not for a warrior
do gm target q
as gm .paragon altar unlock 950002
as q .paragon altar bind 0 3 950002
expect output has does not belong to your class

as q .paragon altar bind 0 3 950007
expect output has is bound to
expect q item 920300 == 0
expect q item 920301 == 0
expect q item 37395 == 1
as q .paragon altar list
expect output has sacrifice bag 0 slot 3: item 37395 enchant 950007

cleanup
do q destroy 37612
do q destroy 37395
do q destroy 920300
do q destroy 920301
